 "text": "9/30/26, 5:12 AM\n\nConfirm your entries.\n\nThe correspondence is created.\n\nExample\nExample 1\n\nA customer informs you that she has recently married and informs you of her new last name. She requests written confirmation\nthat her data has been changed. Once the clerk has entered the new name in the field Last Name (BUTOOO-NAME_LAST) in the\n\ntransaction Change Business Partner , he creates a correspondence that documents the change made and sends it to the\ncustomer.\n\nExample 2\n\nA tenant informs you that the bank details for the collection authorization that you have will change in two months. The clerk\nenters the new bank details in the field Bank Details ID for incoming payments (field FKKVKP-EBVTY) in the transaction Contract\n\nAccount and schedules the change for the date specified. Using the correspondence for master data changes he informs the\ntenant about the change planned in the system.\n\nContract Account and Contract Special Features for IS-U\n\nThis documentation section contains information about enhancements and variations from the FI-CA contract account and\ncontract, which apply specifically to SAP Utilities (IS-U).\n\nContracts (IS-U)\n\nDefinition\n\nContracts in IS-U.\n\nUse\n\nContracts represent the entities that are billed. You can bill one or more contracts together using a contract account.\nStructure\n\nYou can divide the data from contracts into three categories:\n\ne General data\n\ne Data relevant to billing (business)\n\ne Data regarding move-in and move-out.\nIntegration\n\nContracts are linked to installations in |S-U; these installations contain technical data with regard to billing. In the case of a move-\nout, the installation remains and the contract is ended. In the case of the next move-in, a new contract is created and linked to the\n",
